# DHI 2011: complexity-first and open-space research correction

Date: 2026-09-06, Asia/Bangkok. Status: RESEARCH AND DESIGN SPECIFICATION ONLY.

Primary target: DHI 2011, Orris-led. Secondary reference: the user's selected DHP 2025 structural method, not its ingredient list or an authenticated numerical model. Irotyl remains excluded. There is no ingredient-count ceiling.

This record answers the challenge to V5's complexity and open-space behavior. It does not revise the formula, authorize a pour, report a sensory observation, or promote a screening result to proof of beauty, similarity, safety or performance. The existing V5 formula, design sidecar and pour card remain historical design artifacts on HOLD. This is not a completed V6.

## 1. Outcome of the audit

**V5 was relationship-aware, but the complete complexity-first method was not applied. Its open-space behavior was not modeled or measured.**

The current formula has 23 stock lines, compared with V4's 26: 20 shared, six removed and three added. The six removals have individual written reasons. The record does not impose a 23- or 30-material cap. The failure is stopping selection before demonstrating the complete architecture and preservation of its functions, not an undisclosed arithmetic cap.

Eight role headings and individual omission proposals are useful preliminary work. They do not establish the governing DHP method's opposed states, spatial perspective, complete transition ownership, recurrent identity, independent ideal design, source conservation and richer-versus-compressed learning. Nor do they establish that the perfume actually smells simple: that physical outcome remains NOT TESTED.

The strongest correction is therefore not to add an arbitrary number of materials. It is to reopen all missing functions, build a sufficiently rich inventory-independent design, and allow every additional material needed for a demonstrated DHI-linked role. Compression comes after those relationships are tested, not before.

