## 2. Twelve-dimensional method audit

These are design and evidence statuses, not sensory scores or a new automated gate result.

| Dimension | What V5 actually supplies | What remains necessary |
|---|---|---|
| Identity | Orris-led DHI intent and takeover exclusions | Protected identity nucleus; reference-qualified comparison at multiple ages and distances |
| Spatial | Air-around-centre hypothesis | Explicit near body, living middle, outer contour and skin echo; physical distance tested separately |
| Temporal | Five-window screening and intended handoffs | Measured transitions, with no conversion of heuristic times to skin-life claims |
| Textural | Powder, root, cream, textile and wood hypotheses | Simultaneous contrasting textures distinguished from merely greater intensity |
| Relational | Eight useful facets and pair omissions | Connected opposed states, cooperation and interference map |
| Transition | Several materials have handoff roles | Owner, collaborators, transformation and isolated comparison for every interface |
| Anatomical | Root-rich centre is suggested | Defined surface, interior, connective tissue, silhouette and residue |
| Pressure/release | Density versus air is implied | Controlled test of dense root against an open petal edge without erasing either |
| Recurrence | Later iris/root return is intended | Identity recognizable after transformation, not just persistent generic wood or musk |
| Diffusion/fixation | Helpers and headspace screening | Source emission, carrier evolution and receiver-space exposure; fixation not assumed from low VP |
| Hedonic coherence | Liking and drift tests are proposed | Blind ratings of actual blends; no OAV-to-pleasure conversion |
| Legibility under adaptation | Recognized as a risk | Fresh versus previously exposed observers, with exposure history recorded |

Source conservation, donor independence and inventory-independent TARGET / IDEAL are additional governance obligations. V5's prose removal explanations do not replace their complete ledgers. Applying the protocol's completed-successor contract would leave the source-compression requirement unsatisfied. No automated donor or complexity gate was run in this audit.

## 3. What the primary research changes

The literature below was checked against primary records, publisher pages or original manuscripts. These are different experiments addressing different endpoints; they cannot be collapsed into one universal complexity rule.

| Source | Actual evidence | Consequence and limit for this project |
|---|---|---|
| [Laing and Francis, 1989](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2628992/) | Subjects had difficulty identifying constituents as simple mixtures gained components. | Component naming is not mixture discrimination, richness, evolution or useful formula-row capacity. It cannot justify a small-material ceiling. |
| [Le Berre et al., 2008](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18304991/) | Small proportion changes in a three-component pineapple mixture changed typicality, including changes below one component-intensity JND in the tested conditions. | Investigate iris-family proportions and handoffs; this is not an iris recipe or a universal optimal ratio. |
| [Miyazawa et al., 2008](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18283044/) | A vapor-controlled maple-lactone/acid experiment found detection synergy involving individually subthreshold components. | A modeled quiet row is not automatically useless. Equally, this specific detection result does not prove hidden synergy, texture or projection for any DHI row. |
| [Weiss et al., 2012](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3523876/) | Broadly distributed, intensity-equalized odorant mixtures became more similar as component counts increased. Even their 30-component mixtures remained discriminable above chance. | Preserve hierarchy and contrast. This highly specific olfactory-white construction does not impose a 30-stock limit on perfume; natural and commercial-mixture rows are not single molecules. |
| [Lapid, Harel and Sobel, 2008](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18534998/) | Binary-mixture pleasantness depended on component pleasantness and relative perceived intensity. | Measure liking and intensity separately. OAV sums and favorable raw-material descriptions do not establish whole-perfume hedonics. |
| [Frank, Fletcher and Hettinger, 2017](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28641388/) | Selective adaptation changed recognition and masking in controlled mixtures. | Test fresh and previously exposed assessors separately. This is not a fixed adaptation clock for perfume families. |
| [Sinding et al., 2017](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28120877/) | Continuous-exposure habituation varied across 32 odorants and was associated with multiple perceptual and physicochemical properties. | Do not assert universal citrus/floral/musk adaptation minutes. The study's constant exposure is not an evaporating perfume plume. |
| [Sato-Akuhara et al., 2023](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9874024/) | Genetic variation involving ionone- and musk-responsive receptors related to individual perception. | Assessor variation matters. This does not establish a universal Alpha Irone stock-volume ceiling or prove that alternative musks use independent receptors. |
| [Brenna, Fuganti and Serra, 2003](https://comptes-rendus.academie-sciences.fr/chimie/articles/en/10.1016/S1631-0748(03)00087-0/) | The authors' research account describes preparation of ten enantiopure irone isomers and discusses botanical-source differences in natural irone profiles. | An unspecified Alpha Irone product is not a complete description of orris or its stereochemistry. The paper supplies neither this stock's assay nor Dior's formula. |
| [Almeida et al., 2019](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.iecr.9b01004) | Evaporation/permeation modeling was compared with analytical measurements for fragrance chemicals applied to porcine skin. | Distinguish material leaving the source from material remaining or entering a substrate. These measurements do not calibrate this Orris/Tonkarome formulation. |
| [Teixeira et al., 2013](https://aiche.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/aic.14106) | A diffusion-tube model was compared with concentration-versus-distance/time measurements, including an 11-chemical mixture. | An actual spatial model needs transport and receiver conditions, not just equilibrium headspace. A tube is not an occupied ventilated room. |
| [Celani, Villermaux and Vergassola, 2014](https://journals.aps.org/prx/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevX.4.041015) | Turbulent-plume theory predicted intermittent concentration events and their spacing; predictions were tested against simulations and laboratory/field data. | Assess encounters, gaps and movement conditions. The paper studies physical odor signals, not human DHI identity or liking. |
| [Cai et al., 2022](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-022-09450-z) | Downwind plant-volatile profiles varied with sampling position and wind conditions. | Source blend and received blend must not be assumed identical. This is not measured fractionation of our perfume or proof that every compound separates in every room. |
| [Pellegrino et al., 2025, PREPRINT](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12363845/) | Concentration-intensity measurements supported prediction of intensity for defined molecular mixtures. | Promising methodology, not a validated DHI hedonic or open-space predictor. The checked record is a preprint, not a Nature Communications article. |
| [Pellegrino et al., July 2026, PREPRINT](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42465471/) | Across 432 mixtures of 2–10 components, averages of measured component quality profiles explained most descriptions. | Use measured descriptive baselines before claiming extra interactions. This is not linear dosing, OAV addition or DHI validation. |

The 2026 preprint used 115 component odors at multiple dilutions (144 component conditions), not 144 unique molecules. It is not peer reviewed; relevant commercial relationships were disclosed. The older and newer experiments address different endpoints, so a ratio-sensitive effect does not automatically contradict a profile-averaging model.

### Iris identity before accord expansion

The irone research makes product identity a design variable, not a label to flatten. Keep the preferred Orris Liquid as a supplied-product hypothesis; keep the separately stocked Alpha Irone as an independently testable accent. Neither is a certified substitute for the other. AIMI and the ionones provide separate proposed powder/violet relationships; an orris-like commercial material does not become an irone merely because its odor description says iris. An undisclosed supplier base is not a disclosed molecule.

This is why the shortlist distinguishes Orivone from irones, holds Ultralia's opaque identity separately, and does not convert botanical profiles or supplier catalog ranges into the user's lot composition. No candidate is admitted as a historical DHI 2011 constituent on this evidence. Irotyl remains excluded by the user's instruction.

### Unsupported shortcuts retired for this design

- Do not use a constituent-identification limit as a useful-material limit.
- Do not assign a physical projection boundary to a single arbitrary vapor-pressure cutoff.
- Do not infer an Alpha Irone stock-volume cap from musk-receptor literature.
- Do not treat a fixed Hedione percentage as a universal takeover threshold.
- Do not award complexity merely for hidden components, naturalness, high row count, supplier prestige, low VP or high OAV.
- Do not treat missing composition or ODT as a true zero, or a modeled OAV below one as proof of either uselessness or beneficial synergy.

The research supports a wider, better-controlled design search. It does not establish that maximum ingredient count or maximum intensity yields maximum pleasure.

## 4. Why the present simulation cannot answer the open-space question

The local [temporal simulator](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/engine/pipeline/simulator.py:90) explicitly labels its loss rate uncalibrated. Its public call accepts formula, stock dilution, batch volume, temperature, context and time windows, but no airflow, distance, source geometry, movement, receiver location or calibrated source flux.

The [evolving formula state](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/engine/pipeline/formula_state.py:535) retains the base matrix's moles and mass during the temporal update. It therefore does not explicitly simulate progressive ethanol/water depletion. Equilibrium partial pressure is useful screening information, but is not an emission rate into a room.

The existing spatial-architecture module expresses qualitative hypotheses and evidence requirements. It does not supply the missing atmospheric transport calculation. These are claim boundaries, not a proposal to silently change the simulator in a research turn.

The necessary chain is:

**Qualified stock and source mixture → substrate/film emission over time → transport and intermittent encounters → observer exposure and adaptation → identity, texture and liking.**

Each arrow needs separate evidence. A high first-step OAV does not prove a recognizable iris field at the receiver.

For later quantitative work, keep domains explicit: mass ppm w/w belongs to the source; gas mixing ratio and an air ODT belong to a receiver-air OAV. An ethanol-solution ODT cannot silently become an air threshold. Naturals require qualified constituent/composite treatment. OAV remains a screening ratio, not percentage perceived contribution or a calibrated probability of detection.

No distance-specific concentration, OAV, skin life, diffusion radius or projection score is calculated here. The necessary measured inputs are absent.

## 5. Expanded architecture before doses

### One subject, two connected states

The design inference is a single iris subject with two simultaneous aspects: **a cool, dry, violet-root surface under tension**, and **a warm, creamy, cosmetic interior close to skin**. They must remain related while the aromatic/fruit entry changes into powder, wood grain and a recurrent root trace. This is a proposed DHI interpretation, not a confirmed account of the 2011 formula.

The DHP 2025 method supplies the grammar of connected contrasts and recurrent identity. It does not require copying DHP materials, making DHI into DHP, or accepting the repository's unvalidated Sandalore/Polysantol requirements. [Dior's current DHP description](https://www.dior.com/en_int/beauty/products/dior-homme-parfum-E000000226.html) is descriptive context, not a disclosed recipe.

### Role map

The following positions are perfumer's perceptual constructs. They are not literal coordinates or promises that individual molecules occupy separate shells. Actual distance is tested independently.

| Layer | Intended relationship | Existing starting owners, not validated effects | Reopened or expanded options |
|---|---|---|---|
| L01: front glint | Cool aromatic entry with restrained green-fruit light | Lavender, Linalyl Acetate, Coriander, Verdox | Restore the separate Linalool and E2MB questions; compare Phenyl Ethyl Acetate |
| L02: iris surface | Violet movement over earthy root, not a separate violet perfume | Alpha Ionone, Alpha Irone, Orris | Beta Ionone, Dihydro Beta Ionone, Orivone as distinct alternatives |
| L03: living root interior | Rich, irregular root character beneath the surface | Orris, Alpha Irone, Indian Vetiver | Carrot Seed EO; compare Orivone against its camphor risk |
| L04: cosmetic body | Powder with a flower-bearing middle, not flat talc | AIMI, Orris, Ethylene Brassylate | Heliotropal (Piperonal); reopen Mimosa as a controlled alternative |
| L05: soft interior edge | Cream held against the dry outer contour | Ebanol, Isobutavan, provisional Benzyl Salicylate | Reopen Sandalore; compare Delta Decalactone or Hexyl Salicylate only for distinct roles |
| L06: fruit/skin connection | Entry transforms into ambrette-like skin warmth | Verdox, Benzyl Acetate, Ambrettolide | Phenyl Ethyl Acetate, Damascol, reopened Osmanthus, each tested for target drift |
| L07: textile and grain | Powder becomes suede-like texture and recognizable dry wood | Cashmeran, Kephalis, Virginia Cedar, Vetival | Osmanthus or Vertofix; compare rather than automatically stack |
| L08: open outer contour | Outward character remains iris-linked instead of anonymous musk/wood | Hedione and Iso E Super are unproven starting helpers | Cedramber; Habanolide/Romandolide alternatives with separate texture and distance endpoints |
| L09: warm rear contour | Coumarinic/vanillic warmth supports, not replaces, the root | Tonkarome, Isobutavan, Kephalis | Qualified alternatives only; existing Tonkarome composition remains unknown |
| L10: skin/fabric return | Root/powder identity recurs inside the later grain and musk | Orris/ionones alongside cedar, vetiver and Ambrettolide | Clearwood or Vertofix hypotheses; require recognition, not merely persistence |

Benzyl Benzoate retains a vehicle/structural question and earns no automatic olfactory-layer credit. Materials appearing in multiple rows do not create extra independent layers merely by being named twice.

### Transition ownership and recurrence hypotheses

| Interface | Proposed owner and collaborators | Specific comparison and rejection condition |
|---|---|---|
| Glint → iris surface | Linalyl Acetate with aromatic entry and Alpha Ionone | Remove or replace the ester handoff at fixed iris nucleus. A longer lavender opening without a better handoff is not success. |
| Fruit → skin | Ambrettolide with fruit bridge | Compare the present bridge, an alternative bridge and bridge omission. Reject recognizable candy/apricot takeover or mere musk-strength gain. |
| Surface → living root | Alpha Irone with Orris; one root-contrast candidate | Test cool/dry and warm/interior factors separately and together. Reject disconnected violet or camphor dominance. |
| Powder → textile | Cashmeran with AIMI; compare Kephalis/Osmanthus routes | Distinguish a texture change from added woody intensity; muddiness or tobacco takeover fails. |
| Cream → grain | Ebanol with cedar; Sandalore is an alternative | Preserve recognizable grain beside softness; do not call indiscriminate smoothing greater depth. |
| Dense body → open contour | Hedione/Iso E Super as starting support, candidate bridge separately | Test at the receiver. Greater detection with lost iris identity is not improved target-linked projection. |
| Grain → recurrent root | Cedar/vetiver with persistent iris-family relationships | Late blind descriptions must recover iris/root character; generic woody persistence is insufficient. |

Recurrence means an identity returning in a changed context, not a model predicting a material remains. The three proposed returns are aromatic-to-violet, fruit-to-ambrette skin, and powder-to-dry-root grain. All remain unobserved hypotheses.

## 6. Sixteen expanded options, not sixteen automatic additions

These names were checked against the live inventory. Listing is not stock, dose or release qualification. Manufacturer descriptions support material character only; other assignments below are explicitly design hypotheses. None is asserted to be an actual DHI 2011 ingredient.

| Candidate | Target-linked question | Main risk or qualification requirement |
|---|---|---|
| Orivone | Can a distinct earthy root edge preserve iris contrast outside the creamy centre? | IFF describes an earthy, camphoraceous orris character, not simply buttery cream. Camphor takeover is a rejection endpoint. |
| Carrot Seed EO | Can a seed/root nuance connect natural root to dry grain? | Exact lot, composite constituents and threshold uncertainty; seed/spice drift. |
| Beta Ionone | Does a second, distinguishable violet/root emphasis improve movement? | Not an automatic replacement for Alpha Ionone; assessor sensitivity and redundancy need testing. Choose the actual neat or separately prepared stock explicitly. |
| Dihydro Beta Ionone | Does an alternative ionone-family contour improve the interface? | Qualify exact product/grade before molecular assumptions; no receptor-orthogonality claim. |
| Heliotropal (Piperonal) | Can a restrained almond/powder interior make the cosmetic body more dimensional? | Neat solid, not a pourable liquid stock; prepare a labeled, basis-qualified dilution before any volume card. Avoid pastry and flat powder. |
| Phenyl Ethyl Acetate | Can a different fruit/petal handoff replace rather than duplicate the current ester bridge? | Floral takeover and redundancy; not Phenyl Ethyl Alcohol. |
| Damascol (10%) | Can a shaded fruit/petal accent connect entry to skin without candy? | Fraction basis and carrier qualification still required; rose/plum drift. |
| Osmanthus Absolute (10% in DPG) | Does a fruit/violet/suede bridge add a missing relationship? | Reopened predecessor option; fraction basis, lot composition and apricot drift. Do not silently use the volume grade. |
| Mimosa Absolute (10% in DPG) | Does a floral interior keep powder alive instead of flat? | Reopened predecessor option; fraction basis and composition; yellow-flower/honey takeover. |
| Hexyl Salicylate | Is a different floral-film support preferable to the current cosmetic-film helper? | Compare as an alternative; do not infer fixation or projection from low volatility. |
| Cedramber | Can the iris-to-cedar boundary carry recognizable character into the outer field? | IFF's diffusive dry-wood description is not a measured distance guarantee; generic amber/cedar dominance. |
| Vertofix | Can a dry-wood/skin bridge support late root recurrence? | Exact owned trade grade must be qualified; do not silently identify it as another named grade. |
| Habanolide | Does an alternative musk give a useful contour without erasing iris? | Maker supports powerful musky/powdery/earthy character, not unique outward projection. Compare with existing musks. |
| Romandolide | Does its soft musk/balsamic volume perform a distinguishable role? | Reopened predecessor option; manufacturer description does not establish the inherited unique projection claim. |
| Delta Decalactone | Can a small creamy texture make the root interior less planar? | Peach/coconut/gourmand drift; no claim that it belongs to the historical formula. |
| Clearwood | Does a cleaner earthy shadow connect the late root and wood? | Owned neat stock is recorded, but this is not natural patchouli equivalence or proof of historical Dior use. |

Primary product character sources: [IFF Orivone](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/orivone/), [IFF Cedramber](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/cedramber/), [DSM-Firmenich Habanolide](https://studio.dsm-firmenich.com/product/habanolider-pe-947303), and [Firmenich Romandolide sheet](https://www.firmenich.com/sites/default/files/uploads/files/ingredients/marketing-sheet/perfumery/ROMANDOLIDE_979031.pdf).

Ultralia is held outside this defined-material shortlist. Its [supplier certificate](https://www.perfumersworld.com/ifra/COA/6II13551.pdf) describes a proprietary perfume compound with an orris/violet odor; it is not a disclosed pure iris molecule or proof of DHI presence. Irotyl is excluded regardless of inventory availability. Depleted Polysantol is not a current-build option. Guaiacwood's unresolved carrier composition is not silently repaired.

Sandalore, Linalool and E2MB remain additional individually conserved predecessor questions, not forgotten because they are outside the sixteen-option expansion table. None of the six V4 removals is reintroduced automatically.

## 7. Controlled learning plan

### Stage A: qualify the experiment, not just the software

Keep an inventory-independent TARGET / IDEAL and a separate executable inventory build. Freeze each version and its immediate predecessor by hash. Preserve every material/function disposition, source plane and transition; record unavailable roles explicitly. A complete donor-independence manifest and source-conservation check remain prerequisites for a claimed completed successor.

Resolve exact product identity, fraction basis, carrier, delivered stock mass and mixture composition before authoritative concentration arithmetic. For known stock mass fraction f and measured delivered stock mass m, supplied-product mass is f × m; source concentrate ppm w/w is 1,000,000 × f × m / total concentrate mass. Constituent ppm additionally needs a qualified assay. No w/w fraction is converted into active volume by simple multiplication.

Orris and Tonkarome composition/threshold gaps remain data holds; their smell is not declared absent. Check material-specific safety and intended exposure before physical trials. This document supplies no permission for skin application, deliberate room saturation or exposure of bystanders.

### Stage B: opposed-state and interface trials

Use a protected, qualified iris nucleus. Define a cold/dry-contour factor and a warm/interior factor. Compare four coded arms: nucleus, nucleus plus cold, nucleus plus warm, and nucleus plus both. Hold non-test material masses and total finished mass fixed, matching carrier identity and contribution wherever a diluted stock changes. Disclose the necessary odorless-balance adjustment; an omission is never assumed to be a perfectly matrix-invariant intervention.

Next, test the highest-risk interfaces one at a time: root versus camphor, powder versus living floral interior, fruit-to-skin, cream-to-grain, and outer contour with preserved iris. Compare omission and alternative arms; do not spend trials on every theoretical pair before a useful role is observable. The newer linear-profile preprint motivates a measured component/mixture descriptive baseline, with extra interaction tests reserved for reproducible residuals and target-critical interfaces.

Set sensory-relevant levels in the actual matrix after stock qualification; no published pineapple, maple or unrelated musk ratio becomes the iris formula's optimum. Low modeled OAV with poor input data yields DATA HOLD, not an automatic reject. A claimed structural exception still needs a repeatable controlled benefit.

### Stage C: richer versus compressed, after learning

Construct the richer candidate from supported layers with no numerical row ceiling. Then build a deliberately compressed comparator around the same protected nucleus, preserving carrier controls and documenting each removed function. Hide ingredient count from assessors. A whole V4-versus-V5 comparison alone cannot isolate complexity: too many doses and materials differ.

Use at least two independently prepared sets; two aliquots from one master are not independent preparations. Balance presentation order across assessors and sets, use anonymous codes, and collect free description before ratings. Two sets are a minimum replication safeguard, not statistical power or proof of significance. Report sample size, uncertainty, preparation/day effects and individual variation; choose panel size and decision margins from pilot variability before confirmatory testing.

### Stage D: time by distance, then movement

The following is a proposed screening grid, not a published optimal perfume protocol or promised performance envelope:

| Variable | Planned control |
|---|---|
| Source | Weighed application mass on a standardized, qualified blotter or fabric; same exposed area and placement |
| Environment | Log temperature, humidity, ventilation, airflow direction and measured air speed; separate still-room and gentle-flow conditions |
| Ages | 5, 30, 120 and 240 minutes; a separate immediate-opening observation if appropriate |
| Receiver locations | 0.1, 0.5, 1 and 2 metres, with geometry and direction recorded; distance is not an intensity-matching substitute |
| Exposure | Fresh-observer group separated from previously exposed observers; record sniff/exposure history and avoid order confounding |
| Movement | Only after stationary trials, a defined source movement/fabric pass; fixed path, speed and receiver position |
| Blanks | Coded carrier/substrate blanks and background checks; ventilate between trials and confirm carryover clearance |
| Measurement | Separate detection, target identification, description, intensity, texture, liking, harshness, fatigue and intermittency |

The complete grid can cause fatigue. Use balanced subsets across sessions/assessors rather than one person sniffing every cell consecutively. An instrumented source/receiver sampling experiment would quantify transport; sensory ratings alone do not supply chemical concentrations. A diffusion-tube or CFD extension is not an automatic requirement for this first controlled screen, and no new pipeline script is proposed here.

A stronger odor at one metre is not sufficient. The central endpoint is whether iris-linked identity and a coherent contrast are detected and described there, then remain intelligible during later encounters. Analyze liking separately from intensity. A separate intensity-matched characterization may help explain a preference, but must not replace the equal-application performance comparison.

Without an authenticated 2011 reference sample, record only fit to the declared DHI-inspired brief. Neither a modern bottle nor the DHP 2025 reference establishes historical DHI 2011 similarity.

## 8. Decisions the system can learn, and what is still unknown

Future observations should produce row/interface decisions: KEEP, REDOSE OR REDILUTE, REPLACE, REJECT, STRUCTURAL BENEFIT SUPPORTED, DATA HOLD, or NON-INFORMATIVE. Each decision must name the exact versions, conditions, comparison and uncertainty. Save negative results as well as positive ones. Passing an arithmetic or schema test cannot populate a sensory decision.

Current accepted learnings are methodological: the earlier selection did not establish the complete complexity method; the simulator has no receiver-space transport; several simple heuristics overstate the evidence; exact product/stock knowledge and controlled comparisons are necessary. These are repository research learnings, not proof that an AI model has been retrained or that a perfume has been smelled.

Current physical states remain NOT TESTED for identity, depth, pleasure, transitions, projection, sillage, recurrence, stability and skin life. Existing mass, mixture-composition and safety holds are unchanged. This audit did not run a formula pipeline, create a new pour card or rerun the earlier software test suite.

## 9. Verification and provenance

The literature-first skill determined the sequence: local contract/stock review, primary research, then a separately labeled research artifact. The context/cost skills kept the work to targeted local reads and native research; three bounded OpenAI-native read-only lanes independently reviewed method, mixture evidence and open-space evidence. The parent checked the substantive findings against current files and primary sources and is the sole editor of this record.

Plugin Management exposes dependency/permission management rather than a scientific evidence source; no plugin install or permission change was necessary. Primary literature was retrieved with the available native web research tools. No external model-provider delegation, supplier contact, purchase, physical experiment, Git integration or release action occurred.

The companion JSON records source bindings and zero formula modifications. Thirteen focused artifact checks passed: the eleven source hashes were unchanged; the 26 predecessor rows and their original role statements plus three V5-only rows were covered; all sixteen candidate listings matched live inventory; references and claim boundaries were consistent; and no formula or physical observations were created. The repository whitespace check exited successfully with existing LF-to-CRLF advisory warnings. These are artifact consistency checks, not perfume tests.
